  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 105 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nSunday...A cooler cloudy and post-frontal day with ongoing lift up \nand over the LLVL baroclinicity which should be settling off to the \nsouth of the DVN CWA. Increasing north to northeasterly boundary \nlayer(BL) winds with some spotty rain will make for not a very nice \nday with a lot of the area held down in the 60s to low 70s. With the \nupper wave still moving acrs the area, suppose some isolated \nthunderstorms possible as well as nuisance funnels.\n\nMonday through Friday...Quick look at the longer range suggests that \nthe large upper low/wave currently centered over southern ID will \nroll eastward acrs the northern plains and toward the upper MS RVR \nValley through Tuesday. This may keep cloudy, cooler weather going \nacrs the area as well as sctrd showers for the early next week \nperiod. As this upper wave fills and pulls off to the east, there \nmay be a mid week precip lull until medium range ensemble indicated \nnext passing trof brings the next precip chances by Thu night or \nnext Friday. Cooler temp regime still looks to last much of the\nweek.",
